Intermittent deadlocks in Go under high load can be tricky to diagnose, especially when mutexes appear correct. Here are the most common culprits beyond basic mutex issues:

## 1. **Goroutine Leaks (Most Common)**
When goroutines don't terminate and accumulate, they can starve the system.

```go
// BAD - Goroutine leak
func handleRequest() {
    go func() {
        for {
            // Never exits, accumulates
            time.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)
        }
    }()
}

// GOOD - Use context for cancellation
func handleRequest(ctx context.Context) {
    go func() {
        for {
            select {
            case <-ctx.Done():
                return
            default:
                // work
                time.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)
            }
        }
    }()
}
```

