## Common Causes & Solutions

### 1. **Objects/Arrays in Dependencies (Most Common)**

When you include objects or arrays in the dependency array, they create a new reference on every render:

```jsx
// ❌ Problem: New object/array created on every render
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData(data);
}, [data]); // data is a new object/array each time

// ✅ Solution: Use stable references
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData(data);
}, [data]); // This still has the same issue if data changes

// Better solution: Extract the data
const stableData = useMemo(() => data, [data]);

useEffect(() => {
  fetchData(stableData);
}, [stableData]);
```

